---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="Security & Confidentiality Architecture | LIFT DD Operating Platform" 
  description="Built for confidential transactions: cryptographic tenant isolation, dynamic watermarked rendering, tamper-evident audit trails, and zero model-training retention."
>
  <Navbar />
  
  <main class="flex-1 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-16">
      
      <!-- Section 34: Header -->
      <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-4">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">
          Transaction Confidentiality
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-white font-heading tracking-tight">
          Built for confidential transactions.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
          Due diligence involves sensitive financial, legal, corporate and commercial information. LIFT is designed around controlled access, complete traceability and institutional confidentiality.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Core Security Mechanics (Sanitized as per Section 34 & 58) -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        
        <div class="glass-panel-glow rounded-2xl p-6 border border-emerald-500/20 space-y-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-400 font-mono font-bold text-base flex items-center justify-center border border-emerald-500/20">
            🔒
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-heading">Cryptographic Tenant Isolation</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Every transaction environment operates within strict tenant boundaries. Deal room files, cap tables, and audit annotations are partitioned to eliminate cross-tenant data leakage risks.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="glass-panel-glow rounded-2xl p-6 border border-indigo-500/20 space-y-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-500/10 text-indigo-400 font-mono font-bold text-base flex items-center justify-center border border-indigo-500/20">
            🛡️
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-heading">Granular Role-Based Access</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Multi-tier permission policies ensure that external specialists (e.g. tech reviewers or IP lawyers) can only access authorized file subsets, with no access to unrelated financial or tax records.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="glass-panel-glow rounded-2xl p-6 border border-purple-500/20 space-y-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-purple-500/10 text-purple-400 font-mono font-bold text-base flex items-center justify-center border border-purple-500/20">
            📜
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-heading">Immutable Audit Trails</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Every file inspection, query submission, checklist confirmation, and report generation is logged with user identity, exact timestamp, and IP verification for institutional auditability.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- Detailed Defense Specifications -->
      <div class="glass-panel rounded-3xl p-8 sm:p-10 border border-white/10 space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">
          Technical Safeguards & Information Governance
        </h2>
        
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-xs">
          
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-white/5 space-y-2">
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-emerald-300">Dynamically Watermarked Document Rendering</div>
            <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              When confidential agreements or financials are viewed in the browser, an indelible diagonal watermark is dynamically rendered featuring the viewer's verified email, IP address, and exact session timestamp.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-white/5 space-y-2">
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-300">Zero Model-Training Retention</div>
            <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Technology-assisted document parsing operates inside isolated execution runtimes. Customer transaction data and confidential filings are strictly never used to train public or commercial AI models.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-white/5 space-y-2">
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-purple-300">Document Version & Download Controls</div>
            <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Deal administrators maintain centralized authority over file download allowances, print permissions, and revocation of access links whenever transaction stages conclude.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-white/5 space-y-2">
            <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-300">Continuous Security Reviews</div>
            <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Continuous code analysis and vulnerability assessments are integrated into our engineering pipeline. External infrastructure evaluations are performed systematically to uphold transaction integrity.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <!-- Section 34 & 58 Verified Notice -->
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-[11px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          <span class="text-slate-200 font-semibold">Security Governance Notice:</span>
          LIFT applies institutional information security standards across encryption in transit and at rest, access controls, and operational separation. Formal third-party attestation reports and independent audit certifications are reviewed systematically with qualified enterprise stakeholders under non-disclosure agreements.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Security Inquiries -->
      <div class="text-center pt-8 border-t border-white/10 space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-heading">
          Confidentiality or Security Questions?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">
          Our security architecture team is available for technical reviews:
        </p>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <a href="mailto:security@lift.business" class="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-emerald-400 font-mono text-xs hover:text-emerald-300 hover:bg-white/10 transition-all inline-block">
            security@lift.business
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
